@node Overview
@chapter Overview

The @samp{tlon-bib} module provides a comprehensive suite of tools for working with Bib@TeX{} bibliographic data. It covers abstract fetching and management (from CrossRef, Google Books, Zotra, and AI), batch abstract processing, entry movement between fluid and stable Bib@TeX{} files, field manipulation (database tags, language identifiers, URL population, journal title fields), citation key generation, citation conversion and replacement (including AI-powered workflows), abstract translation via DeepL, reporting on entry quality, and entry creation from Markdown YAML front matter.

The module integrates with several external packages including @samp{ebib}, @samp{citar}, @samp{zotra-extras}, @samp{gptel}, and @samp{tlon-ai} to provide a seamless bibliography management experience. Most commands work in both @samp{bibtex-mode} and Ebib modes, dispatching to the appropriate field accessor functions automatically.

You can access all the major commands through the transient menu @code{tlon-bib-menu} (@ref{Transient menu}).

