@node Abstract overwrite behavior
@section Abstract overwrite behavior

@vindex tlon-abstract-overwrite
The user option @code{tlon-abstract-overwrite} controls what happens when you fetch an abstract for an entry that already has one. Its default value is @samp{ask}, which prompts you interactively each time. You can set it to @samp{always} to silently overwrite existing abstracts, or to @samp{never} to skip entries that already have an abstract without prompting.

This option affects @code{tlon-fetch-and-set-abstract} (@ref{Fetch and set abstract}) and the batch abstract processing command @code{tlon-batch-set-abstracts} (@ref{Batch set abstracts}).

@node AI model for citation replacement
@section AI model for citation replacement

@vindex tlon-bib-replace-citations-model
The user option @code{tlon-bib-replace-citations-model} specifies the AI model used by @code{tlon-bib-replace-citations-in-file} (@ref{Replace citations in file}) to identify and replace bibliographic citations with structured @samp{<Cite>} tags. The value is a cons cell whose car is the backend name (a string) and whose cdr is the model symbol. For example:

@lisp
(setq tlon-bib-replace-citations-model '("Gemini" . gemini-pro-latest))
@end lisp

When set to @code{nil}, the default @code{gptel-model} is used. See @code{gptel-extras-ai-models} for available backend and model combinations.

@node AI model for adding missing citations
@section AI model for adding missing citations

@vindex tlon-bib-add-missing-citations-model
The user option @code{tlon-bib-add-missing-citations-model} specifies the AI model used by @code{tlon-bib-add-missing-citations} (@ref{Add missing citations}) to locate and add bibliographic entries for citations marked as missing. Its format and semantics are the same as @code{tlon-bib-replace-citations-model} (@ref{AI model for citation replacement}). By default, it inherits the value of @code{tlon-bib-replace-citations-model}.

@node Maximum concurrent citation replacements
@section Maximum concurrent citation replacements

@vindex tlon-bib-replace-citations-max-concurrent
The user option @code{tlon-bib-replace-citations-max-concurrent} controls how many files are processed simultaneously when running @code{tlon-bib-replace-citations-in-org-files-in-directory} (@ref{Replace citations in Org directory}). The default is 5. Increase it if your system can handle more parallel AI requests; decrease it if you encounter rate limits or resource constraints.

