@node Move entry to fluid
@subsection Move entry to fluid

@findex tlon-move-entry-to-fluid
The command @code{tlon-move-entry-to-fluid} moves the Bib@TeX{} entry at point (or a specified key) from its current file to the fluid Bib@TeX{} file (@code{tlon-file-fluid}). After moving, it adds the @samp{database} field set to ``Tlon'' and copies the citation key to the kill ring for convenient pasting.

@node Move all fluid entries to stable
@subsection Move all fluid entries to stable

@findex tlon-move-all-fluid-entries-to-stable
The command @code{tlon-move-all-fluid-entries-to-stable} transfers all entries from @samp{fluid.bib} to @samp{stable.bib} in a single operation. It requires both files to be saved before proceeding. After the move, @samp{fluid.bib} is emptied. You will typically want to commit these changes to version control afterward.

@node Add database field
@subsection Add database field

@findex tlon-add-database-field
The command @code{tlon-add-database-field} iterates over every entry in a specified Bib@TeX{} file and adds or updates the @samp{database} field to ``Tlon''. This is useful for tagging entries that belong to the Tlon bibliography.

@findex tlon-auto-add-database-field
The function @code{tlon-auto-add-database-field} is intended for use in @samp{after-save-hook}. Whenever the fluid Bib@TeX{} file is saved, it automatically runs @code{tlon-add-database-field} on that file.

@node Auto-clean entry
@subsection Auto-clean entry

@findex tlon-auto-clean-entry
The command @code{tlon-auto-clean-entry} is a hook function for @samp{after-save-hook} in Bib@TeX{} mode. On each save, it removes trailing spaces in fields, escapes special characters (@samp{$}, @samp{%}, @samp{#}, @samp{&}), and runs @code{bibtex-clean-entry} if point is at the start of an entry. It skips cleaning on the upstream database file (@code{tlon-file-db-upstream}).

@node Add language identifiers
@subsection Add language identifiers

@findex tlon-add-lang-id-to-entries
The command @code{tlon-add-lang-id-to-entries} iterates through entries in the current Bib@TeX{} buffer. For each entry missing a @samp{langid} field, it prompts you to select a language using @code{tlon-select-language} and sets the field accordingly.

@node Swap colon character in title
@subsection Swap colon character in title

@findex tlon-bib-swap-colon-in-title
The command @code{tlon-bib-swap-colon-in-title} toggles between the standard colon character (@samp{:}) and the Unicode modified letter colon (@samp{꞉}, U+A789) in the @samp{title} field of a Bib@TeX{} entry. This is useful because Bib@TeX{} treats the colon as a separator between title and subtitle, so the modified letter colon can be used to avoid unintended splitting. The command prompts for a Bib@TeX{} key, jumps to the entry, performs the swap, and saves the file.

@node Unescape characters
@subsection Unescape characters

@findex tlon-bib-unescape-escaped-characters
The command @code{tlon-bib-unescape-escaped-characters} reverses the escaping performed by @code{bibtex-extras-escape-special-characters}. For each character in @code{bibtex-extras-escaped-characters}, it replaces the backslash-escaped form (e.g., @samp{\$}) with the literal character (e.g., @samp{$}). It operates on a specified file or the current buffer, and reports the number of replacements made.

@node Remove URL fields
@subsection Remove URL fields

@findex tlon-bib-remove-url-fields-with-doi
The command @code{tlon-bib-remove-url-fields-with-doi} removes the @samp{url} field from every entry in the current Bib@TeX{} buffer that also has a @samp{doi} field. This is useful for cleaning up redundant URL fields when a DOI is available. With a prefix argument, the buffer is saved after modification.

@findex tlon-bib-remove-url-fields-with-isbn
The command @code{tlon-bib-remove-url-fields-with-isbn} does the same but for entries that have an @samp{isbn} field instead of a DOI@.

@node Create Bib@TeX{} original
@subsection Create Bib@TeX{} original

@findex tlon-create-bibtex-original
The command @code{tlon-create-bibtex-original} adds a new original Bib@TeX{} entry to the fluid file by calling @code{zotra-extras-add-entry}.

@node URL management
@section URL management

@menu
* Prompt to add missing URLs::
