@node Prompt to add missing URLs
@subsection Prompt to add missing URLs

@findex tlon-prompt-to-add-missing-urls
The command @code{tlon-prompt-to-add-missing-urls} scans the current Markdown buffer for URLs that are not present in the Tlon bibliography. For each missing URL, it highlights it and prompts you to decide whether to add it. The URLs you approve are saved to a file for subsequent import via @code{zotra-extras-add-multiple-urls}.

@node Populate URL field
@subsection Populate URL field

@findex tlon-bib-populate-url-field
The command @code{tlon-bib-populate-url-field} constructs and sets the @samp{url} field for the Bib@TeX{} entry at point. The URL is built from three components: the base URL for the entry's language from the ``uqbar'' subproject, the articles path for that language, and a slugified version of the title. If the entry already has a @samp{url} field, you are prompted before overwriting.

@findex tlon-bib-populate-url-fields-in-language
The command @code{tlon-bib-populate-url-fields-in-language} extends this to all entries in the language of the entry at point. It collects all article files from the corresponding site directory, reads their Bib@TeX{} keys from YAML front matter, and populates the @samp{url} field for each matching entry.

@node Populate journal title fields
@subsection Populate journal title fields

@findex tlon-bib-populate-journaltitle-fields-in-language
The command @code{tlon-bib-populate-journaltitle-fields-in-language} sets the @samp{journaltitle} field for all Bib@TeX{} entries in the language of the entry at point. The journal title value is computed once by looking up the site's homepage title for the appropriate language. Existing values trigger a confirmation prompt before overwriting.

@node Translation entry creation
@section Translation entry creation

@menu
* Create Bib@TeX{} translation::
* Create translations from directory::
@end menu

@node Create Bib@TeX{} translation
@subsection Create Bib@TeX{} translation

@findex tlon-create-bibtex-translation
The command @code{tlon-create-bibtex-translation} creates a new Bib@TeX{} entry representing a translation of the entry at point. It works in @samp{bibtex-mode}, @samp{ebib-entry-mode}, and @samp{ebib-index-mode}.

The command prompts for a target language (or accepts a two-letter code programmatically). It then translates the title and abstract via DeepL, generates a new key by appending the capitalized language code to the original key, and populates fields including @samp{langid}, @samp{title}, @samp{author}, @samp{journaltitle}, @samp{translation} (the original key), @samp{abstract}, and @samp{date}. In Ebib, it switches to the translations database (database 3) and creates the entry there. The @samp{url} field is then populated via @code{tlon-bib-populate-url-field} (@ref{Populate URL field}).

@node Create translations from directory
@subsection Create translations from directory

@findex tlon-bib-create-translations-from-dir
The command @code{tlon-bib-create-translations-from-dir} iterates over all Markdown files in a directory (defaulting to the current directory). For each file, it reads the YAML @samp{original_key} and @samp{title}, jumps to the corresponding Bib@TeX{} entry, calls @code{tlon-create-bibtex-translation}, overrides the new entry's @samp{title} with the YAML title (if present), and regenerates the @samp{url} field based on the updated title.

@node Entry creation from Markdown
@section Entry creation from Markdown

@menu
* Create entry from Markdown::
@end menu

@node Create entry from Markdown
@subsection Create entry from Markdown

@findex tlon-bib-create-entry-from-markdown
The command @code{tlon-bib-create-entry-from-markdown} creates a Bib@TeX{} entry in the database file (@samp{db.bib}) from the YAML front matter of the current Markdown buffer. It populates the @samp{title}, @samp{author} (from @samp{authors}, reversed to ``Last, First'' format), @samp{translator} (from @samp{translators}), @samp{langid} (from the repository's language), @samp{date}, and @samp{translation} (from @samp{original_key}). The Bib@TeX{} key is constructed by appending the capitalized two-letter language code to the @samp{original_key}. After insertion, the @samp{url} field is populated via @code{tlon-bib-populate-url-field} (@ref{Populate URL field}).

@findex tlon-bib-create-entries-in-dir
The command @code{tlon-bib-create-entries-in-dir} applies @code{tlon-bib-create-entry-from-markdown} to every Markdown file in a directory. It continues on errors and reports a summary of created, skipped, and failed entries.

