@end menu

@node Replace citations in file
@subsection Replace citations in file

@findex tlon-bib-replace-citations-in-file
The command @code{tlon-bib-replace-citations-in-file} uses an AI agent to identify and replace all bibliographic citations in a file with structured @samp{<Cite>} tags. The agent is provided with tools to search the bibliography, fetch web content, perform web searches, and edit the file. Citations that cannot be found are enclosed in @samp{@{!} and @samp{!@}} markers for later processing.

When called from Dired with marked files, it processes all marked files. When called with an active region, it processes the current file. Otherwise, it prompts for a file. Files are processed in batches of @code{tlon-bib-replace-citations-max-concurrent} (@ref{Maximum concurrent citation replacements}).

The AI model used is controlled by @code{tlon-bib-replace-citations-model} (@ref{AI model for citation replacement}).

@node Replace citations in Org directory
@subsection Replace citations in Org directory

@findex tlon-bib-replace-citations-in-org-files-in-directory
The command @code{tlon-bib-replace-citations-in-org-files-in-directory} runs @code{tlon-bib-replace-citations-in-file} on every @samp{.org} file in a specified directory (non-recursively). Files are processed in batches; the next batch starts only after all files in the current batch have finished.

@node Add missing citations
@subsection Add missing citations

@findex tlon-bib-add-missing-citations
The command @code{tlon-bib-add-missing-citations} instructs an AI agent to process a file or region and find all citations marked as missing (enclosed in @samp{@{!} and @samp{!@}}). For each, the agent uses search tools to find an identifier (URL, DOI, or ISBN), adds a corresponding entry to the fluid bibliography file via the @samp{add_bib_entry} tool, and replaces the marked citation with a proper @samp{<Cite>} tag.

The AI model used is controlled by @code{tlon-bib-add-missing-citations-model} (@ref{AI model for adding missing citations}).

