@node Entries report
@subsection Entries report

@findex tlon-bib-entries-report
The command @code{tlon-bib-entries-report} generates a report buffer listing Bib@TeX{} entries in the current buffer that have problems with their abstracts. It categorizes entries into four groups: those with no abstract, those with abstracts shorter than @code{tlon-min-abstract-length} words, those with abstracts longer than @code{tlon-max-abstract-length} words, and those with abstracts of fewer than 10 words. Entries in @code{tlon-bib-excluded-keys} (@ref{Excluded keys management}), entries with a @samp{crossref} field, and translation entries (those with a @samp{translation} field) are filtered out.

@node Excluded keys management
@subsection Excluded keys management

@findex tlon-bib-add-to-excluded-keys
The command @code{tlon-bib-add-to-excluded-keys} adds one or more Bib@TeX{} keys (as a space-separated string) to the @code{tlon-bib-excluded-keys} list and persists them to @code{tlon-bib-excluded-keys-file}. These keys are excluded from the entries report (@ref{Entries report}).

@node Find entry with missing field
@subsection Find entry with missing field

@findex tlon-bib-find-next-entry-with-missing-field
The command @code{tlon-bib-find-next-entry-with-missing-field} moves point to the next Bib@TeX{} entry in the buffer that is missing a specified field. It prompts for the field name with completion from @code{bibtex-extras-biblatex-fields} and skips entries that have a @samp{crossref} field.

@node Transient menu
@section Transient menu

@findex tlon-bib-menu
The command @code{tlon-bib-menu} activates a transient menu providing quick access to the commands in this module. It is organized into three columns:

@itemize
@item
@strong{Markdown}: URL management (@samp{m f}, @samp{m z}), citation conversion (@samp{m b}, @samp{m l}), key checking (@samp{m c}), AI citation replacement (@samp{m r}, @samp{m R}, @samp{m a}), and model selection (@samp{m -r}, @samp{m -a}).
@item
@strong{Ebib}: abstract fetching (@samp{e a}), translation entry creation (@samp{e c}), URL population (@samp{e u}, @samp{e U}), and journal title population (@samp{e J}).
@item
@strong{Bib@TeX{}}: reporting (@samp{b g}, @samp{b x}), entry movement (@samp{b t}, @samp{b s}), URL field removal (@samp{b d}, @samp{b i}), and colon swapping (@samp{b :}).
@end itemize

