@node Mode guards
@section Mode guards

@findex tlon-ensure-bib
The function @code{tlon-ensure-bib} signals a @samp{user-error} unless the current buffer is in @samp{bibtex-mode}, @samp{ebib-entry-mode}, or @samp{ebib-index-mode}. Use it at the start of commands that require a Bib@TeX{}-related context.

@findex tlon-ensure-bibtex
The function @code{tlon-ensure-bibtex} is a stricter variant that signals an error unless the buffer is specifically in @samp{bibtex-mode}.

@node Key retrieval
@section Key retrieval

@findex tlon-get-key-at-point
The function @code{tlon-get-key-at-point} returns the Bib@TeX{} key at point, dispatching to the appropriate backend function depending on whether you are in Ebib or @samp{bibtex-mode}.

@node Bibliography lookup
@section Bibliography lookup

@findex tlon-bibliography-lookup
The function @code{tlon-bibliography-lookup} searches the cached Tlon bibliography (via @samp{citar-cache--bibliographies}) for an entry where a specified field matches a given value. It can optionally perform substring matching and return a different field from the matching entry. This is the central lookup mechanism used by many commands in this module.

@findex tlon-get-field-in-bibliography
The function @code{tlon-get-field-in-bibliography} returns a list of all values for a specified field across all entries in the cached bibliography. It signals an error if no bibliographies are cached.

@findex tlon-bib-get-keys-in-file
The function @code{tlon-bib-get-keys-in-file} returns a list of all Bib@TeX{} keys in a specified file by accessing the citar cache. It ensures the file is cached if not already present.

@node Abstract translation helpers
@section Abstract translation helpers

@findex tlon-read-abstract-translations
The function @code{tlon-read-abstract-translations} reads and parses the per-language JSON abstract translations file for a given language code or name, returning an alist of @samp{(KEY . TEXT)} pairs.

@findex tlon-write-abstract-translations
The function @code{tlon-write-abstract-translations} writes an alist of @samp{(KEY . TEXT)} pairs to the per-language JSON file. It creates the directory if needed.

@findex tlon-add-abstract-translation
The function @code{tlon-add-abstract-translation} adds or updates a translation for a given key in the per-language store. When a variable is provided instead of a language, the alist is updated in memory rather than written to disk.

@findex tlon-get-abstract-translation
The function @code{tlon-get-abstract-translation} retrieves the translated abstract for a specific Bib@TeX{} key and language code from the per-language JSON file.

@node Autokey generation
@section Autokey generation

@findex tlon-generate-autokey
The function @code{tlon-generate-autokey} generates a Bib@TeX{} citation key from author, year, and title strings. It respects the standard Bib@TeX{} autokey settings (separators, name count, year length, title word count) and optionally applies @code{bibtex-autokey-before-presentation-function}.

@node Reporting helpers
@section Reporting helpers

@findex tlon-bib-load-excluded-keys
The function @code{tlon-bib-load-excluded-keys} loads the excluded keys list from @code{tlon-bib-excluded-keys-file} into @code{tlon-bib-excluded-keys}.

@findex tlon-bib-save-excluded-keys
The function @code{tlon-bib-save-excluded-keys} persists the current @code{tlon-bib-excluded-keys} list back to its file.

@node Miscellaneous helpers
@section Miscellaneous helpers

@findex tlon-abstract-cleanup
The function @code{tlon-abstract-cleanup} cleans a raw abstract string by removing XML/HTML tags, @LaTeX{} formatting artifacts, and extraneous leading words like ``summary'' or ``abstract''. It also ensures the string ends with a period.

@findex tlon-bib-remove-braces
The function @code{tlon-bib-remove-braces} strips curly braces from a string, which is useful before sending Bib@TeX{} text to external services like DeepL@.

@findex tlon-fetch-url-from-doi
The function @code{tlon-fetch-url-from-doi} resolves a DOI to its final redirect URL using @samp{curl}.

@findex tlon-bib-add-multiple-urls-from-file
The function @code{tlon-bib-add-multiple-urls-from-file} reads a file containing URLs (one per line), filters out those already in the bibliography, and calls @code{zotra-extras-add-multiple-urls} to add the rest to the fluid file.

